# vesc-dashboard: ESP32-S3 additions (Waveshare ESP32-S3-Zero, env s3zero_deadman_uart). ESP-IDF
# applies this file right after sdkconfig.defaults whenever the target is esp32s3, and after
# every file in SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS the matching "<file>.esp32s3" if one exists (the 'ble'
# fragment needs none). A value already in the generated sdkconfig.<env> wins over this file:
# after editing it delete sdkconfig.s3zero_deadman_uart.
#
# Both cores, split by job (include/config.h checks every value below):
#   core 0 (TASK_CORE_RADIO): the BLE controller, the NimBLE host and the ble task, plus
#          ESP-IDF's own system tasks;
#   core 1 (TASK_CORE_APP): app_main (the supervisor) and every other task of this firmware,
#          so the UART / I2C / RMT / TWAI interrupts they install land there as well.
# The firmware's own tasks therefore share one core with exactly the priorities they have on
# the single-core C6 (TASK_PRIO_DEADMAN above everything, every worker above the supervisor);
# what moved is the radio, whose tasks at priorities 21 / 23 no longer preempt them.
CONFIG_ESP_MAIN_TASK_AFFINITY_CPU1=y
CONFIG_BT_CTRL_PINNED_TO_CORE_0=y
CONFIG_BT_NIMBLE_PINNED_TO_CORE_0=y
CONFIG_ESP_DEFAULT_CPU_FREQ_MHZ_160=y
